27.
RESOLUTION
Authorizing the Cheyenne Board of Public Utilities to discharge
uncollectible debts pursuant to Wyoming Statute 16-4302. (SPONSOR
— DR. RINNE)
Mr. Moody moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Roybal. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Brad Bowen, Board of Public Utilities Administrator, provided a staff report and committee
member Roybal commented on the item.
28.
LEASES/CONTRACTS/LEGAL:
d)
Contract between the City of Cheyenne and Companion Life for Stop Loss
Insurance for city employees. (Various City Funds)
Dr. Rinne moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Moody. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote,
Danin Ilass, Human Resources Director, provided a staff report and advised representatives from
the City’s consultant, Novo Benefits, were also available for questions.
Committee member
Roybal commented on the item.
e)
Professional Services Agreement between the City of Cheyenne, Cheyenne Board
of Public Utilities and McGee, Ilearne & Paiz (MHP), LLP to provide financial and
compliance auditing services for the fiscal year ending June 30, 2025. (General
Fund)
Mr. Moody moved to approve in an amount not to exceed $103,350.00, seconded by Mr. Roybal.
Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
