f)
Professional Services Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and TDSi
— The
Design Studio, inc., for the South Lions Park Dunbar Field Improvements Design
Services project. (2021 Specific Purpose Option Tax Fund and Rec Mill Grant)
Dr. Rinne moved to approve in an amount not to exceed $86,912.00, seconded by Mr. Moody.
Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Jason Sanchez, Community Recreation & Events Director, provided a staff report and noted Randy
Byers, TDSi
The Design Studio, inc., was available for questions.
Chairman Laybourn and
committee member Roybal commented on the item.
g)
Contract between the City of Cheyenne and the Wyoming Game and Fish
Commission by and through the Wyoming Game and Fish Department to allow
public access for hunting, without charge, to the Hunter Management Area located
on the Belvoir Ranch. (Revenue to the City)
Mr. Roybal moved to approve in an amount not to exceed $40,655.00, seconded by Mr. Moody.
Motion carried with Dr. Rinne and Mr. Roybal voting “YES” and Mr. Moody abstaining from
voting on the item.
Vicki Nemecek, Public Works Director, provided a staff report.
Chairman Laybourn and
committee members Moody and Rinne commented on the item. There was additional discussion
surrounding the decision by Mr. Moody to “abstain” from voting and previous goveming body
practices.
h)
Memorandum of Understanding between the City of Cheyenne and Frog Creek
Partners to define responsibilities with each party associated with the installation
and maintenance of Gutter Bins installed within the city.
Mr. Roybal moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Moody. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Tom Cobb, City Engineer, provided a staff report. Brian Deurloo, Frog Creek Partners, provided
additional information and requested consideration of modifications to the memorandum of
understanding. Chairman Laybourn and committee members Rinne and Roybal commented on
the item.
29.
